      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-5057",
      ":question/problem": "An office typist was given the task to transfer all the work documents to the company's internal system. The following table shows some statistics on the process.\n\n| **$t\\,\\text{(hour)}$** | $4\\text{th}$ | $5\\text{th}$ | $6\\text{th}$ | $7\\text{th}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${D}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{(documents/hour)}$ | $11$ | $8$ | $7$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThe typist transfers the documents at a rate of ${D}^{\u2032}(t)$, where ${D}^{\u2032}(t)$ is measured in documents per hour. At the end of the seventh hour, $t=7$, the typist had completed $50$ documents. Use the tangent line approximation of $D$ at time $t=7$ to determine the number of documents transferred after the ninth hour."
